{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_013BfdpT6maJgMFiELtbw9m4","type":"tool_result","content":"cissy.c\ncsvfield.c\ncsvfield.h\ncsvline.c\ncsvline.h\ndoc\nMakefile\nrange.c\nrange.h\n---\nMakefile\ntest_csvfield.c\ntest_csvline.c\ntest_range.c\n---\ncissy\n=====\ncommand-line csv processing and formatting utility/tool.\n\nAWK, sed, cut and other popular/common utilities can handle a \nmajority of tasks, but cissy is specifically written to for CSV\nfiles where the quoted text contains the field separator.\n\nSee the [man page](https://github.com/slass100/cissy/wiki/man-page) in the \nWiki for help.\n\n\nSome basic examples are shown in the man page.\n\nThings cissy can do easily:\n\n##### Change delimiters without changing quoted text\n```bash\n$ echo '1,\"2,3\",4,5' | cissy -do :\n\n1:\"2,3\":4:5\n```\n\n##### Move/transpose columns\n```bash\n$ echo 'a,b,c,d,e,f' | cissy -c 4-\n\nd,e,f\n```\n\n```bash\n$ echo 'a,b,c,d,e,f' | cissy -c 1-3,5-\n\na,b,c,e,f\n```\n\n\n```bash\n$ echo 'a,b,c,d,e,f' | cissy -c 4\n\nd\n```\n\n##### Use filenames or stdin/stdout\n\n```bash\n$ cat inputfile.txt | cissy -c 4\n\n$ cissy -i inputfile.txt -c 4\n```","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"849d3a89-2d42-4f57-abbc-8e2985cfa2d0","uuid":"fc3203c5-3c27-450a-9ab5-f955e787f41f","timestamp":"2026-05-29T17:23:15.599Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"cissy.c\ncsvfield.c\ncsvfield.h\ncsvline.c\ncsvline.h\ndoc\nMakefile\nrange.c\nrange.h\n---\nMakefile\ntest_csvfield.c\ntest_csvline.c\ntest_range.c\n---\ncissy\n=====\ncommand-line csv processing and formatting utility/tool.\n\nAWK, sed, cut and other popular/common utilities can handle a \nmajority of tasks, but cissy is specifically written to for CSV\nfiles where the quoted text contains the field separator.\n\nSee the [man page](https://github.com/slass100/cissy/wiki/man-page) in the \nWiki for help.\n\n\nSome basic examples are shown in the man page.\n\nThings cissy can do easily:\n\n##### Change delimiters without changing quoted text\n```bash\n$ echo '1,\"2,3\",4,5' | cissy -do :\n\n1:\"2,3\":4:5\n```\n\n##### Move/transpose columns\n```bash\n$ echo 'a,b,c,d,e,f' | cissy -c 4-\n\nd,e,f\n```\n\n```bash\n$ echo 'a,b,c,d,e,f' | cissy -c 1-3,5-\n\na,b,c,e,f\n```\n\n\n```bash\n$ echo 'a,b,c,d,e,f' | cissy -c 4\n\nd\n```\n\n##### Use filenames or stdin/stdout\n\n```bash\n$ cat inputfile.txt | cissy -c 4\n\n$ cissy -i inputfile.txt -c 4\n```","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
